	(text "D1-D12 are all SML-P11VT (red, 0.2 mm, Vf 1.8 V at 1 mA). No series resistors: at 1.8 V\nthe GPIO drivers limit the current and PWM sets brightness. Layout decides which ones\nglow straight through the skin (back glow) and which face into the light channel to light\nthe engraving (edge lit); electrically they're identical."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.7 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2d6de7a5-9144-4e71-84da-0f1c794265be")
	)
	(text "8-pin MSPM0: PA0/PA1 are open-drain only, so they take I2C. PA1 is also NRST, and R2 is its\nboot pull-up. Firmware reassigns NRST to PA1 for I2C, so SWD is the only way back in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "558e3a68-e8d8-49c1-8dff-eec520d26111")
	)
	(text "L3/L4 share SWCLK/SWDIO. Firmware waits about 1 s after reset before driving them as LED\nlines, so a probe can still attach on bench power. Program through TP1-TP6 before lamination."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "74c260e9-cbea-4950-9bc6-d1fcc486efe9")
	)
	(text "Field meter: no divider. The harvest output holds 1.8 V until the field can't keep up, so\nI read VDD/3 on the internal supply-monitor channel and raise LED duty until it starts to\nsag. The duty where it sags tracks field strength."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "996cff65-cc6a-41c3-bae9-e40ee5f2ede9")
	)
